# catalog/lane-run-inputs.d/watchdog-responder.ro — what one
# `bin/watchdog-responder.sh $p` run reads and never writes back. The
# file:line after each entry is where the run reads it. The inventory is in
# docs/notes/2026-10-14-BH-6720-llm-alert-lanes-offhub.md.
#
# The run reads state/stale-owed.json (bin/watchdog-responder.sh:217), not
# logs/ALERTS.log, and model-route.sh only appends to it. It rides as the
# lines that name the project as a whole token.
@lines logs/ALERTS.log (^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.-])$p([^A-Za-z0-9_.-]|$)
logs/ALERTS.log (this project's lines only)
# bin/watchdog-responder.sh:217-220. One JSON object keyed by project: it
# rides whole (every project's entry), and the run keeps its own (line 220).
state/stale-owed.json
# bin/watchdog-responder.sh:274-283
state/build-queue/$p/*.json
# bin/watchdog-responder.sh:284
state/fly-pool/$p/*.json
# bin/lib/llm-lane-project.sh (llp_arm), bin/watchdog-responder.sh:322,385
fleet.conf
# bin/watchdog-responder.sh:78,144, bin/lib/lane-gate.sh:238, bin/lib/alert-state.sh:57
flags/*
